<section>
<p><strong>Chapter 1: The Lantern Keeper</strong></p>
<p>Mara kept the lantern on the northern pier for eleven winters.</p>
<p>Every evening she trimmed the wick, wrote the weather in her ledger, and counted the boats home.</p>
<p>Accents survive conversion: café, naïve, façade. So do other scripts: Ελληνικά, Русский, 日本語.</p>
<p><image l:href="#img_1"/></p>
<p>Skip ahead to the ending.</p>
</section>
<section>
<p><strong>Chapter 2: The Ledger</strong></p>
<p>The ledger recorded wind, tide and the names of every vessel that passed the breakwater.</p>
<p>Its last page was blank except for a single line: see the final chapter.</p>
</section>
<section>
<p><strong>Chapter 3: The Final Chapter</strong></p>
<p><emphasis>On the last night of the eleventh winter, every boat came home before dark.</emphasis></p>
</section>
